Protocol
A protocol is a set of rules, like traffic rules on the road. Everyone follows the same rules, so everything works.

iP_internet-Protocol
internet Protocol is the set of rules for sending data from one device to another on a network. 
The IP address is only one part of it.

why?,
Imagine 1,000 different companies make phones, laptops, and routers. 
If each one used its own rules, they could not talk to each other.
IP gives one common rule to all of them. So any device can talk to any other device in the world.

For-What?,
Think about sending a big parcel by post
Cut into small pieces. Big data is broken into small pieces called packets.
Put the address on each piece. Each packet gets the sender's address and the receiver's address.
Send. The packets travel through many routers, each one passing it forward.
Join at the end. The receiver collects all the pieces.

What-for?
Opening websites
WhatsApp and video calls
YouTube and online games
Email
Everything on the internet

What IP does NOT do?,
IP only delivers. It does not check if the data arrived safely. 
Another protocol, TCP, does that job. This is why we say TCP/IP together.
